# What the deployment serves is a plain static folder. Everything listed below
# stays in git, because the tools and the image sources are how this build is
# reproduced, but it is kept out of the upload so it is never readable at the
# public URL.
#
# vercel.json is deliberately NOT listed: it configures the deployment.

# Build and QA tooling. Only a reviewer running the checks needs these.
tools/

# Review documents.
*.md

# Local-only config and the CLI link.
.gitignore
.vercelignore
.vercel/

# QA artefact: the cutout composited on navy, regenerated by tools/cutout.py.
# README section 2 describes it as "never served"; this line is what makes that
# true, since the CLI uploads the working directory rather than the git tree.
images/_portrait-preview.png

# Image sources. The page only ever requests the optimised .webp files;
# tools/cutout.py and tools/optimize_images.py read these locally.
images/portrait.jpg
images/portrait.png
images/portrait-cutout.png

# Defence in depth: the unredacted CV, with the referees' numbers and the
# covering letter, must never be uploaded even if a local copy reappears. It is
# already in .gitignore, but the CLI uploads the working directory, not the git
# tree, so a stray local file would otherwise be served.
assets/Sim-Soklim-CV-original.pdf
